{"title":"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Markus has 9 candies and Katharina has 5 candies. Sanjiv gives away a total of 10 candies to Markus and Katharina so that Markus and Katharina each end up with the same total number of candies. How many candies does Markus have now?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of candies that Sanjiv gave to Markus. Since Sanjiv gave away <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> candies in total, this means Sanjiv gave <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/e/fce4726a5a736e9e7d2f5fcf4dc5846ffa8374e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 - c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> candies to Katharina. Markus and Katharina ended up with the same total of candies, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52f7f4a5b7856dd2556313fae151f05960e4ae4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + c = 5 + 10 - c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/9802902bba14a95e23758e27cc85fd54b9b58069.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c + 9 = 15 - c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3ed17390b01123fc0e2aebfc460e8b3cec28c19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c + c = 15 - 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/85705d734e2fdba72fc17422f179a435771c4c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/1/0216b1740411fca1c2b5d544c1184831df396af1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac{6}{2} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>This means that Markus ended up with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accad1fc0307b6d5b98b0810b0e687c81f803161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + 3 = \\boxed{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" /> candies.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At first, Markus and Katharina have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5acfd0500aed8693be0ec7fcf4e6d5e0c4949053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + 5 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> candies in total. Since Sanjiv gives away a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> candies, this means that there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/8/9f8e12d1ff9a4c0c0cb1482b6b39eae7ed301609.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 + 10 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> between the two.\n</p><p>Each person has the same total, so this means that Markus has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/6252cfbb5cf79ff4e2c13ef8182163793fa6ff6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{24}{2} = \\boxed{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" /> candies.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC\" title=\"2020 CSMC\">2020 CSMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Senior_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Senior Competition\">CEMC Senior Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018063003\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.074 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 114/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1240/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 137/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2363/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7